\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-180\li180\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1\cf0 .If we allow our God to guide us,
\par \pard\li180\sl180\slmult0 And hope in Him thro' all our ways,
\par He'll give us strength what e'er betide us
\par And bear us thro' the evil days.
\par Who trusts in God's unchanging love
\par \i Builds on the rock that cannot move.
\par \i0 
\par \pard\fi-180\li180\sl180\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. What can our anxious cares avail,
\par \pard\li180\sl180\slmult0 Our never ceasing moans and sighs?
\par What can it help us to bewail
\par Each painful moment as it flies?
\par Our cross and trials do but press
\par \i The heavier for our bitterness.
\par \i0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl180\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Thou knows when joyful hours are best
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 And sends them as Thou sees it meet.
\par When I have borne the fiery test
\par And am made free from all deceit,
\par Thou comes to me all unaware
\par \i And makes my own Thy loving care!
\par \i0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Help me my restless heart to still
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj And wait in cheerful hope, content
\par To take what e'er Thy gracious will,
\par Thy all discerning love, hath sent;
\par Nor doubt my inmost wants are known
\par \pard\li315\sl180\slmult0\qj\i To Him who chose me for His own.
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\i0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl180\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5.  Help me to swerve not from Thy ways,
\par \pard\li315\sl180\slmult0 But do my own part faithfully
\par And trust Thy promises of grace
\par That they may be fulfilled in me.
\par Thou never will forsake in need
\par \pard\li315\sl180\slmult0\qj\i The soul that trusts in Thee indeed.
\par \pard\i0\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

